# Giott's trigger is for "another Dwarf you control" and "an Equipment you control". Bot1 declines the trigger of Giott itself on turn 1 (Choose() with an empty answer: the
# graveyard stays empty). Bot2's Magda (a Dwarf) and Skullclamp (an Equipment) enter on turn 2 and ask Bot1 nothing: not "you control" (the stack is empty once it has resolved). On turn 3 Bot1's own
# Ornithopter, neither a Dwarf nor an Equipment, asks nothing (the stack is empty once it has resolved; the casts below are its positive controls), while Magda and then Skullclamp each ask Bot1: it
# discards an Island and draws another each time (CR 603.6a, 701.9), so two Islands are in the graveyard and the hand is down by the two cards cast.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Giott, King of the Dwarves
